// known-issues §20/§24/§25: unbounded recursion is a diagnostic on BOTH
// backends, not a crash. A Cx call is a native recursion in the interpreter and
// a native recursion in compiled code alike, so this used to take the process's
// stack either way — the interpreter at exit 127 (the parity harness's SKIP
// sentinel, so a death looked like an unsupported construct) and the JIT at
// 0xC00000FD (not even 127, so it parity-failed outright).
//
// This fixture could not exist until both guards landed: whichever backend
// still crashed, the rejection-shape harness correctly refused to call a crash
// a rejection. That it lands now is the proof the pattern is closed.
fnc: t64 boom(n: t64) { boom(n + 1) }
print(boom(0))
